Road Safety Data
----------------

Dataset: collisions (20,901 personal injury collisions the Metropolitan
Police and the City of London Police recorded in 2025, one point each)

Publisher: the Department for Transport, "Road safety open data" (STATS19:
personal injury collisions on public roads reported to the police in Great
Britain), its page last updated on 30 July 2026, "2025 final data added".
https://www.gov.uk/government/statistical-data-sets/road-safety-open-data

Licence: Open Government Licence v3.0 (OGL-UK-3.0), under which the
publisher's page says its content is available.
https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/

Credit: Department for Transport. Contains public sector information
licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.

Where and when: read on 2026-10-12 from the publisher's own files:

  https://data.dft.gov.uk/road-accidents-safety-data/dft-road-casualty-statistics-collision-2025.csv
  (19,349,153 bytes, SHA-256 e699c19bdb82e47e449b6f3381ac87631865f6a31cef118c9955ba80ca870e2b)
  https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6ab2a71d997a4b2950cced58/dft-road-casualty-statistics-road-safety-open-dataset-data-guide-2025.xlsx
  (the open dataset's data guide, 85,112 bytes, SHA-256 51b08606ef3dad1ae5d4c8726241b022fc8e4bbdc910ef0e5cc2fb92b054fc12)

Kept: of the 101,525 collisions of 2025, the 20,901 recorded by police
forces 1 (Metropolitan Police) and 48 (City of London), whose areas
together are Greater London; for each, its collision reference, date,
time, severity, road type, speed limit and light conditions, the coded
values decoded with the data guide, and its place from the file's
longitude and latitude. Severity is as the police recorded it (the file's
collision_severity), not the DfT's adjusted estimate. Nothing else of the
record is kept.


The workflow's results
----------------------

The template carries each workflow step's result from its run on
2026-10-12 (results/<step id>.parquet): the collisions with their H3 cells,
those that killed or seriously injured someone, their count per cell,
every cell with its count, and the hot spot scores. They are made from the
Road Safety Data and carry its terms.


